{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ஆ","gloss":"adjectival suffix"}],"gloss":"conversing"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கவலை","parts":[{"text":"கவலை","lemma":"கவலை","gloss":"anxiety"}],"gloss":"anxiety"},{"surface":"மாக்கட்டி","parts":[{"text":"மாக்கட்டி","lemma":"மாக்கட்டி","gloss":"of the people"}],"gloss":"of the people"},{"surface":"பேதை","parts":[{"text":"பேதை","lemma":"பேதை","gloss":"foolish"}],"gloss":"foolish"},{"surface":"ஊரே","parts":[{"text":"ஊர்","lemma":"ஊர்","gloss":"town"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"the town indeed"}]}],"literal":"Wearing leaf-garment loins bearing not-capable-of / entering small waist to-distress as / beautiful soft bosom fully swelling / round striped breasts with-casket competed / \"How will she become, she of flower-like ear-ornaments?\" saying / with distressed heart conversing / anxious people's foolish town indeed.","translation":"Her round, striped breasts have swelled to fully fill her beautiful, soft bosom, competing with metal caskets, so that her slender, small waist can no longer bear the weight of her leaf-garment-clad loins, causing her distress. \"What will become of her, who wears flower-like ear-ornaments?\" so wonders the foolish town of anxious people, conversing with distressed hearts.","modern":"தழையினாலான ஆடையை அணிந்த அவளது அல்குல் பகுதியைத் தாங்க முடியாமல், அவளது மிகச் சிறிய இடை வருந்தும்படியாக, அவளது அழகிய மென்மையான மார்பில் முழுமையாகப் பருத்து வீங்கி, அவளது திரண்ட வரிகளையுடைய முலைகள் செப்புப் பாத்திரங்களோடு போட்டியிடுகின்றன. \"பூப்போன்ற காதணிகளை அணிந்த இவள் இனி என்ன ஆவாளோ?\" என்று துன்பப்படும் நெஞ்சத்தோடு தங்களுக்குள் பேசிக்கொள்ளும் கவலை நிறைந்த மக்கள் வாழும் அறிவற்ற ஊர் இது.","explanation":"The friend (தோழி) is speaking about the heroine's physical maturity, mockingly describing the townspeople's unnecessary anxiety. The heroine has grown into full womanhood, and her breasts have become full and heavy like metal caskets, making her waist seem too thin to bear the weight of her leaf-garment. Seeing this transition, the simple-minded townspeople are filled with worry, wondering how such a delicate girl will survive this heavy physical transformation. This belongs to the Kuriñci landscape, where the transition to youth and love is marked by physical changes. The contrast between the heavy, casket-like breasts and the thread-like waist is a classic motif of feminine beauty, and the town's collective anxiety highlights their naive protective nature. Key words include நுசுப்பு (waist), முலை (breasts), செப்பு (casket), and கவலை மாக்கள் (anxious people).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}